.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Vt X509_STORE
structure is intended to be a consolidated mechanism for holding
information about X.509 certificates and CRLs, and constructing and
validating chains of certificates terminating in trusted roots.
It admits multiple lookup mechanisms and efficient scaling performance
with large numbers of certificates, and a great deal of flexibility in
how validation and policy checks are performed.
.Pp
Details of the chain building and checking process are described in
.Xr openssl-verification-options 1
and
.Xr openssl-verification-options 1 .
.Pp
.Xr X509_STORE_new 3
creates an empty
.Vt X509_STORE
structure, which contains no information about trusted certificates or
where such certificates are located on disk, and is generally not
usable.
Normally, trusted certificates will be added to the
.Vt X509_STORE
to prepare it for use, via mechanisms such as
.Fn X509_STORE_add_lookup
and
.Xr X509_LOOKUP_file 3 ,
or
.Xr PEM_read_bio_X509_AUX 3
and
.Fn X509_STORE_add_cert .
CRLs can also be added, and many behaviors configured as desired.
.Pp
Once the
.Vt X509_STORE
is suitably configured,
.Xr X509_STORE_CTX_new 3
is used to instantiate a single-use
.Sy X509_STORE_CTX
for each chain-building and verification operation.
That process includes providing the end-entity certificate to be
verified and an additional set of untrusted certificates that may be
used in chain-building.
As such, it is expected that the certificates included in the
.Vt X509_STORE
are certificates that represent trusted entities such as root
certificate authorities (CAs).
OpenSSL represents these trusted certificates internally as
.Vt X509
objects with an associated
.Sy X509_CERT_AUX ,
as are produced by
.Xr PEM_read_bio_X509_AUX 3
and similar routines that refer to X509_AUX. The public interfaces that
operate on such trusted certificates still operate on pointers to
.Vt X509
objects, though.
.Pp
.Fn X509_STORE_add_cert
and
.Fn X509_STORE_add_crl
add the respective object to the
.Vt X509_STORE Ns 's
local storage.
Untrusted objects should not be added in this way.
The added object's reference count is incremented by one, hence the
caller retains ownership of the object and needs to free it when it is
no longer needed.
.Pp
.Fn X509_STORE_set_depth ,
.Fn X509_STORE_set_flags ,
.Fn X509_STORE_set_purpose ,
.Fn X509_STORE_set_trust ,
and
.Xr X509_STORE_set1_param 3
set the default values for the corresponding values used in certificate
chain validation.
Their behavior is documented in the corresponding
.Sy X509_VERIFY_PARAM
manual pages, e.g.,
.Xr X509_VERIFY_PARAM_set_depth 3 .
The
.Vt X509_STORE
.Sy MUST NOT
be NULL.
.Pp
.Fn X509_STORE_add_lookup
finds or creates a
.Xr X509_LOOKUP 3
with the
.Xr X509_LOOKUP_METHOD 3
.Fa meth
and adds it to the
.Vt X509_STORE
.Fa store .
This also associates the
.Vt X509_STORE
with the lookup, so
.Vt X509_LOOKUP
functions can look up objects in that store.
.Pp
.Fn X509_STORE_load_file_ex
loads trusted certificate(s) into an
.Vt X509_STORE
from a given file.
The library context
.Fa libctx
and property query
.Fa propq
are used when fetching algorithms from providers.
.Pp
.Fn X509_STORE_load_file
is similar to
.Fn X509_STORE_load_file_ex
but uses NULL for the library context
.Fa libctx
and property query
.Fa propq .
.Pp
.Fn X509_STORE_load_path
loads trusted certificate(s) into an
.Vt X509_STORE
from a given directory path.
The certificates in the directory must be in hashed form, as documented
in
.Xr X509_LOOKUP_hash_dir 3 .
.Pp
.Fn X509_STORE_load_store_ex
loads trusted certificate(s) into an
.Vt X509_STORE
from a store at a given URI. The library context
.Fa libctx
and property query
.Fa propq
are used when fetching algorithms from providers.
.Pp
.Fn X509_STORE_load_store
is similar to
.Fn X509_STORE_load_store_ex
but uses NULL for the library context
.Fa libctx
and property query
.Fa propq .
.Pp
.Fn X509_STORE_load_locations_ex
combines
.Fn X509_STORE_load_file_ex
and
.Fn X509_STORE_load_path
for a given file and/or directory path.
It is permitted to specify just a file, just a directory, or both paths.
.Pp
.Fn X509_STORE_load_locations
is similar to
.Fn X509_STORE_load_locations_ex
but uses NULL for the library context
.Fa libctx
and property query
.Fa propq .
.Pp
.Fn X509_STORE_set_default_paths_ex
is somewhat misnamed, in that it does not set what default paths should
be used for loading certificates.
Instead, it loads certificates into the
.Vt X509_STORE
from the hardcoded default paths.
The library context
.Fa libctx
and property query
.Fa propq
are used when fetching algorithms from providers.
.Pp
.Fn X509_STORE_set_default_paths
is similar to
.Fn X509_STORE_set_default_paths_ex
but uses NULL for the library context
.Fa libctx
and property query
.Fa propq .
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn X509_STORE_add_cert ,
.Fn X509_STORE_add_crl ,
.Fn X509_STORE_set_depth ,
.Fn X509_STORE_set_flags ,
.Fn X509_STORE_set_purpose ,
.Fn X509_STORE_set_trust ,
.Fn X509_STORE_load_file_ex ,
.Fn X509_STORE_load_file ,
.Fn X509_STORE_load_path ,
.Fn X509_STORE_load_store_ex ,
.Fn X509_STORE_load_store ,
.Fn X509_STORE_load_locations_ex ,
.Fn X509_STORE_load_locations ,
.Fn X509_STORE_set_default_paths_ex
and
.Fn X509_STORE_set_default_paths
return 1 on success or 0 on failure.
.Pp
.Fn X509_STORE_add_lookup
returns the found or created
.Xr X509_LOOKUP 3 ,
or NULL on error.
